xnu 0252: a mapped buffer of many MiB is not written back every submission

gpusubtime=1 answers the question the frame line could not: of an 8.0 ms
submission, 7.8 ms is bufferSync, and it writes back 84 MB of buffers the task
holds a mapping of -- the two 23 MB surfaces the compositor renders into plus
everything else it touched. Those bytes are the GPU's writes: the CPU never
wrote them, the GPU has to read them back, and the panel copy already
invalidates the surface it reads (mondrian_fb_clean), so the writeback buys
nothing and costs the largest slice of the frame.

gpusyncmapmax=<KiB> caps it: a mapped buffer larger than that is written back
only when it is a command stream or the kernel wrote it. At 8192 the two
display surfaces stop being written back and the small ones (the poster,
textures, the staging blob, command buffers of a few KiB) are treated exactly
as before, so a CPU-written texture still reaches the CP. 0 is the old rule.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianGPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianGPU.cpp
@@ -157,6 +157,29 @@
 }
 
 /*
+ * gpusyncmapmax=<KiB>: a mapped buffer larger than that is written back only
+ * when it is a command stream or the kernel wrote it, not because the task
+ * holds a mapping of it. Measured with gpusubtime=1: a submission wrote back
+ * 84 MB of mapped buffers in 7.8 ms of an 8.0 ms call, and the two 23 MB
+ * surfaces the compositor renders into are most of it -- bytes the CPU never
+ * wrote, which the GPU then reads back. The panel copy invalidates what it
+ * reads (mondrian_fb_clean), so the display surface needs no writeback here.
+ * Zero keeps the old rule: every mapped buffer is written back.
+ */
+static uint32_t
+mondrian_sync_map_max(void)
+{
+	static int parsed;
+	static uint32_t limit;
+
+	if (parsed == 0) {
+		parsed = 1;
+		(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("gpusyncmapmax", &limit, sizeof(limit));
+	}
+	return limit;
+}
+
+/*
  * Whether a submission must write a buffer back depends on who can have
  * written it since the last writeback:
  *
@@ -1462,6 +1485,7 @@
 	 * write into.
 	 */
 	syncStart = mach_absolute_time();
+	const uint32_t map_max = mondrian_sync_map_max() << 10;
 	for (i = 0; i < request->nr_bos; i++) {
 		mondrian_buffer *bo = bufferForType(bos[i].handle);
 		bool stream = false;
@@ -1476,7 +1500,8 @@
 				stream = true;
 			}
 		}
-		if (fSyncAll || stream || bo->dirty || bo->mapped) {
